      "releaseNotes": "Correlate 2.5 is a new Dashboard, and it works in light mode.\n\n• Recovery, Strain and Sleep lead the page as three rings, with the morning verdict and your HRV right under them.\n• Vitals — respiratory rate, resting heart rate, HRV, SpO2, wrist temperature and sleep — each checked against your own recent range, so \"Normal\" means normal for you.\n• Strain is rebuilt from your heart rate minute by minute, so a hard session counts as one. Workouts show up in the Strain detail with their source.\n• Every score is now a tile: Body & Recovery, Zone 2, workouts, sleep consistency, sleep debt and everything that used to live under More. Tap any tile for the full detail.\n• A month calendar of daily Recovery, Strain and Sleep scores, from the calendar button on the Dashboard.\n• Light mode. Correlate follows your iPhone, or pick Light or Dark under Data Sources › Appearance.\n• The daily journal is its own tab, and it explains at the bottom how your answers feed the correlation analysis.\n• Your verdict appears from day one, computed from the Apple Health history you already have; the 14-day countdown only applies to your first correlation report.\n• A shorter first launch: connect Apple Health, optionally pick what you want to figure out, done.\n• Mood, food, hydration and symptom logging have left the Dashboard. Existing entries are untouched.\n• Data Sources › Privacy: a switch to turn off anonymous usage statistics. Your health data never leaves your iPhone either way.",
